notes: 'Imported from microbedecoder (source_id=kgmicrobe.compound:fastidious_anaerobe_broth_with_meat_granules);
  no CAS-RN or CHEBI/NCIT match. Curator review needed. Follow-on source review: The
  authentic imported label names meatgranules in FAB, not a whole Oxoid cooked-meat
  medium. Primary EOLabs overlay and Acumedia granule documentation show broth/material
  separation and that granules can themselves be formulated products. Neogen and DSMZ/Oxoid
  FAB recipes differ; no source link selects either for this MicrobeDecoder owner.
  Retain named meatgranules without guessing tissue, cookingstate, productcatalog
  or FOODON skeletal-food identity. The other inherited peptone,starch,glucose parts
  are not newly approved; the current Neogen comparator lacks starch/glucose and cannot
  retrospectively select the unspecified original formula. Legacy first-part assertion
  retained here as provenance, not active grounding: {"component_name": "meat (cooked)",
  "component_id": "FOODON:03305103", "reference_scope": "MIM_CATALOG", "source": "microbedecoder
  research decomposition (#213/#308)"}. Successor dependency assessment: The original
  Falsen 2005 methods/results text associates Fastidious Anaerobe Broth with Oxoid.
  Its separately named Anaerobe Systems peptone/yeast/glucose fermentation broth is
  a different preparation and supplies no FAB recipe. The Neogen NCM0199 sheet is
  a LabM/Neogen product comparator, unselected for this source. Original Oxoid catalogue/formula
  and the historical peptone material remain unresolved. The existing meat-granule
  withdrawal is retained; starch/glucose and other inherited component claims are
  unchanged and remain unverified. No claim that peptone is absent is made. Withdraw
  the unsupported peptone component_id and set reference_scope UNMAPPED; retain its
  existing component_name as historical interpretation, not a newly observed expanded
  source label. The original assertion method and UNKNOWN/PARTIAL completeness remain
  unchanged. This is a bounded part-reference correction only. Whole-owner identity,
  raw labels, occurrence counts, quantities, unrelated components, all historical
  evidence and source/role/export holds are preserved. Historical all-components-identified
  statements describe prior states, not a new approval. No new MappingEvidence is
  added; historical human/component evidence enums are not rewritten.'
